# Assertions checked during the replay, so an agent can verify its own work
# without reading a state dump by eye.
#
# What this run does: five rooms, each a wave the arena spawns. Clear one, take
# one of three upgrades from the seeded stream, and the next wave arrives. Two
# base spells held together evolve into a third.

# The run reached the last room and finished it.
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:room == 5
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:run_complete == true

# Every enemy across all five waves died: two, three, four, four and seven.
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:kills == 20
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:enemy_count == 0

# Spells are spawned nodes rather than a pool, and there were a lot of them.
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:fired > 400

# The upgrades the seeded stream offered combined into an evolution. This is
# §12's requirement: a replay must reproduce the same spell evolution.
tick 2599 /Arena01 var:evolved == Forking Arc

# Waves arrive one room at a time rather than all at once.
tick 900 /Arena01 var:enemy_count > 0
tick 900 /Arena01 var:room < 5

# The player survived the run.
tick 2599 /Arena01/Player exists == true
